      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Playing Urza's Saga on turn 1 instead of Seat of the Synod is debatable. Urza's Saga only produces colorless mana on chapter I, and it will be sacrificed after chapter III (turn 3). Meanwhile, Seat of the Synod produces blue mana permanently and counts as an artifact for Mox Opal's metalcraft. With Mox Opal and Mishra's Bauble in hand, playing Seat of the Synod first would let the player deploy Mox Opal and Mishra's Bauble this turn, immediately reaching 3 artifacts (Seat + Opal + Bauble) to activate metalcraft. This would enable casting Pinnacle Emissary via Warp ({U/R}) as early as turn 1 with the colored mana from Opal. Playing Urza's Saga first delays metalcraft activation and colored mana access. However, Urza's Saga does have a strong payoff if it survives to chapters II and III, and the opponent has Wasteland in their deck which could destroy either land. The Saga is also vulnerable to Wasteland, so leading with it into an unknown opponent is risky.",
