    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Mox Opal before Mishra's Bauble is slightly suboptimal sequencing. With Urza's Saga (chapter I), Seat of the Synod in hand, and these two 0-cost artifacts, the player needs 3 artifacts for Metalcraft. Playing Mishra's Bauble first allows immediate activation (tap + sacrifice to look at opponent's top card and draw next upkeep), getting value before it could be lost. Mox Opal can't tap for mana yet anyway since Metalcraft isn't active (only 2 artifacts: Urza's Saga enchantment land + Mox Opal). Playing Bauble first, activating it, then playing Mox Opal would give the same board position but with Bauble's scry/draw effect secured. However, sacrificing Bauble would leave only 2 artifacts (Urza's Saga + Mox Opal), so Metalcraft still wouldn't be online. The sequencing matters because Bauble's value is time-sensitive - you want to use it as early as possible to get the delayed draw sooner.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Mox Opal before Mishra's Bauble",
      "better_line": "Cast Mishra's Bauble first, activate it immediately to look at opponent's top card and queue up a draw for next upkeep, then cast Mox Opal. This gets the Bauble's delayed draw trigger one turn sooner at no cost.",
