      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Lavaspur Boots before Urza's Bauble is a sequencing error. Urza's Bauble costs {0} and is an artifact, which matters for Mox Opal's Metalcraft threshold (needs 3 artifacts). Currently MiniMx has Mox Opal, Seat of the Synod, and Urza's Saga (enchantment, not artifact) on the battlefield - so only 2 artifacts. Playing Urza's Bauble first would bring the artifact count to 3 (Mox Opal, Seat of the Synod, Urza's Bauble), enabling Metalcraft on Mox Opal before spending mana on Lavaspur Boots. Additionally, Urza's Bauble provides information and a delayed draw at no cost. By casting Boots first, the artifact count goes to 3 anyway (adding Boots), but playing the free spell first is strictly better sequencing - it gives information from Bauble's activated ability and could enable Mox Opal mana to be used for other things. Also, the reasoning mentions 'trample' and 'prowess' which are not abilities on Pinnacle Emissary or granted by Lavaspur Boots (Boots gives +1/+0, haste, and ward {1}), suggesting confused card evaluation.",
